   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the correction law, in relation to authorizing the Schenectady county correctional facility to also be used for the detention of persons under arrest being held for arraignment in any court located in the county of Schenectady",
    "basePrintNo": "S4518",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4518-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§500-a & 500-c, Cor L",
    "lawSection": "Correction Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4518\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the correction law, in relation to authorizing the\nSchenectady county correctional facility to also be used for the\ndetention of persons under arrest being held for arraignment in any\ncourt located in the county of Schenectady\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nRelates to authorizing the Schenectady county correctional facility to\nalso be used for the detention of persons under arrest being held for\narraignment in any court located in the county of Schenectady.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 - Amends Section 500-a of the Correction Law by adding\nsubdivision 2-n that allows the Schenectady County jail to detain\npersons under arrest being held for arraignment in any court in\nSchenectady County.\n\nSection 2 - Amends Section 500-c of the Correction Law by adding a\nsubdivision 20 to provide that in Schenectady County all provisions of\nthe section shall apply equally in any case where the sheriff is\nholding a person under arrest for arraignment prior to commitment as\nif such person had been judicially committed to the custody of the\nsheriff and such person may be held in the Schenectady county\ncorrectional facility\n\nSection 3 is the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Schenectady County Legislature is requesting legislation, which\nwould permit the use of the Schenectady County jail by various police\nagencies as a holding cell for pre-arraigned prisoners. This would\nallow for the best utilization of county resources and staff\nallocations.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided further, that the\namendments to section 500-c of the correction law, as made by section\ntwo of this act, shall not affect the repeal of such section and shall\nbe deemed repealed therewith.\n\n",
